      "problem": "Which diversity training programs at United Internet address unconscious bias and inclusive work culture?",
      "solution": "Diversity training courses, overview of the topics of diversity, reduce the influence of unconscious bias, trained at least 80% of the workforce, unconscious thought processes, voluntary two-part diversity training course",
      "attempt": "As of my last update in October 2023, I don't have specific information on the exact diversity training programs offered by United Internet that address unconscious bias and inclusive work culture. However, many companies implement similar programs to foster an inclusive environment and combat unconscious biases. These programs often include:\n\n1. **Unconscious Bias Training**: This type of training helps employees recognize their own biases and understand how these biases can affect decision-making processes in the workplace.\n\n2. **Inclusive Leadership Workshops**: These workshops focus on developing leadership skills that promote inclusivity and ensure all team members feel valued and heard.\n\n3. **Diversity and Inclusion Workshops**: These sessions educate employees about the importance of diversity and inclusion, providing strategies for creating a more inclusive workplace.\n\n4. **Cultural Competency Training**: This training aims to improve employees' understanding of different cultures and backgrounds, enhancing their ability to interact effectively with colleagues from diverse backgrounds.\n\n5. **Safe Space Training**: Creating safe spaces where employees can discuss issues related to diversity and inclusion without fear of judgment or retribution.\n\nTo get detailed information about the specific programs offered by United Internet, you might want to visit their official website or contact their HR department directly. They may also provide this information through internal communications or during employee orientation sessions.",
