      "problem": "Where does the CA Immo Group fulfill its tax obligations across its operational footprint?",
      "solution": "Austria, Czechia, Germany, Hungary, Netherlands, Poland, Serbia, Switzerland",
      "attempt": "CA Immo Group, as a multinational real estate company, fulfills its tax obligations in various jurisdictions where it operates. The company is headquartered in Vienna, Austria, and has a significant presence in other European countries such as Germany, France, and Poland. As a result, CA Immo must comply with local tax laws and regulations in each of these locations.\n\nHere's how CA Immo likely manages its tax obligations:\n\n1. **Corporate Income Tax**: In each country where CA Immo owns or manages properties, it pays corporate income tax on profits generated from its operations within that jurisdiction. The rates and rules for corporate income tax vary by country.\n\n2. **Real Estate Taxes**: Depending on the country, CA Immo may be subject to property taxes or real estate taxes based on the value of the properties it owns or rents out.\n\n3. **Value-Added Tax (VAT)**: CA Immo also needs to collect VAT on rental income and sales of properties in countries where VAT applies, and remit this to the respective tax authorities.\n\n4. **Withholding Tax**: If CA Immo pays dividends or interest to shareholders or lenders located outside the country of operation, withholding tax might apply, which would need to be managed according to international tax treaties and local laws.\n\n5. **Transfer Pricing**: For transactions between subsidiaries or affiliates in different countries, CA Immo must ensure compliance with transfer pricing rules to avoid penalties and disputes with tax authorities.\n\n6. **Local Registration and Compliance**: CA Immo must register with local tax authorities in each country where it operates and maintain compliance with all local tax reporting requirements.\n\nTo manage these obligations effectively, CA Immo likely employs a team of tax professionals or works with external tax advisors who specialize in cross-border tax issues. This ensures that the company remains compliant with all relevant tax laws and regulations across its operational footprint.",
