      "problem": "Which specific social support services are provided to employees in Germany through United Internet's Employee Assistance Program?",
      "solution": "care for relatives, childcare, clinics, financial crises, medical assistance, parental counseling, therapists",
      "attempt": "United Internet, like many large companies, offers an Employee Assistance Program (EAP) designed to help employees deal with personal and work-related issues that may impact their performance and well-being. However, the specifics of the EAP can vary from company to company. For United Internet, the Employee Assistance Program typically includes a range of services aimed at supporting employees' mental health and overall well-being. Here are some common types of services that might be included:\n\n1. **Counseling Services**: Confidential counseling sessions for employees dealing with personal or professional issues. These can include stress management, relationship problems, grief, and other emotional concerns.\n\n2. **Work-Life Balance Support**: Resources and advice on managing work-life balance, including tips on time management, family care, and personal development.\n\n3. **Legal and Financial Advice**: Access to legal and financial advisors who can provide guidance on personal matters such as wills, estate planning, debt management, and legal disputes.\n\n4. **Health and Wellness Programs**: Information and resources related to physical and mental health, including fitness programs, nutrition advice, and smoking cessation support.\n\n5. **Stress Management Workshops**: Training sessions focused on techniques to manage stress effectively, which can improve both personal and professional life.\n\n6. **Career Development**: Guidance and resources for career advancement, including resume writing, interview preparation, and job search strategies.\n\n7. **Substance Abuse Counseling**: Support for those struggling with substance abuse, including referrals to specialized treatment centers if necessary.\n\n8. **Conflict Resolution**: Assistance in resolving conflicts within the workplace or personal relationships.\n\n9. **Referral Services**: Connections to external professionals and organizations for more specialized needs, ensuring employees have access to a wide range of support services.\n\nIt's important to note that the exact offerings can vary, and the best way to get detailed information about the specific services offered by United Internet's Employee Assistance Program would be to contact the HR department directly or visit their official website for the most up-to-date and accurate information.",
