      "id": "test:000516:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "problem": "Which categories of emissions are covered under Scope 3 in ESG reporting?",
      "solution": "Scope 3, business travel, external data centres, office paper, purchase of IT equipment, staff commuting",
      "attempt": "Scope 3 emissions, as defined by the Greenhouse Gas (GHG) Protocol, cover all indirect emissions that occur in a company’s value chain and not from sources that the company owns or controls. These emissions are categorized into 15 different categories, which can be broadly grouped into upstream and downstream activities. Here is a breakdown of these categories:\n\n### Upstream Activities (Categories 1-11)\n1. **Purchased Goods and Services**: Emissions from the production of goods and services purchased by the company.\n2. **Capital Goods**: Emissions from the manufacture of equipment and buildings used by the company.\n3. **Fuel- and Energy-Related Activities**: Emissions from the extraction, production, and transportation of fuels and energy consumed by the company.\n4. **Upstream Transportation and Distribution**: Emissions from transporting and distributing goods to the company.\n5. **Waste Generated in Operations**: Emissions from waste generated by the company's operations.\n6. **Business Travel**: Emissions from travel by employees for business purposes.\n7. **Employee Commuting**: Emissions from employees commuting to work.\n8. **Upstream Leased Assets**: Emissions from leased assets used by the company.\n9. **Investments**: Emissions related to investments made by the company.\n10. **Use of Sold Products**: Emissions from the use of products sold by the company.\n11. **End-of-Life Treatment of Sold Products**: Emissions from the disposal or recycling of products sold by the company.\n\n### Downstream Activities (Categories 12-15)\n12. **Downstream Transportation and Distribution**: Emissions from transporting and distributing goods from the company to customers.\n13. **Processing of Sold Products**: Emissions from further processing of products sold by the company.\n14. **Fueled and Energy-Related Activities by Sold Products**: Emissions from the use of fuel and energy in products sold by the company.\n15. **Leased Assets**: Emissions from assets leased out by the company.\n\nThese categories help companies understand their full impact on the environment beyond their direct operations, providing a comprehensive view of their carbon footprint.",
      "grading": "No"
    },
