        "paragraph": "$\\begin{array}{l} \\bigstar \\text{ Classification in higher risk class compared to previous report}\\\\ \\text{Classification in same risk class compared to previous report}\\\\ \\text{Classification in lower risk class compared to previous report}\\\\ \\text{— Risk or risk category no longer exists} \\end{array}$ \n- 14 Business model and organisational structure\n- 16 Corporate strategy and goals\n- 19 Corporate management\n- 24 Economic environment\n- 27 Overview of the course of business\n- 38 Report on opportunities and risks\n- 49 Non-financial group statement 84 Corporate governance and other disclosures\n- 2023 Annual report Back to contents\nThe Executive Board has an overview of the risk situation presented through the implemented risk management process and monthly reporting. Various market, IT, tax, financial, strategic and operational risks were identified as of 31 December 2023. No significant risks were identified.\nThe Executive Board classifies the potential effects on the general future development of freenet and the financial and non-financial performance indicators as low overall. The Executive Board expects that the positive development of freenet AG forecast in the outlook (see report on expected developments) will not be significantly impaired by the risks identified. Overall, it can be assumed that the risks will not have any effects on the continued existence of freenet AG.",
