      "attempt": "To gain insights into freenet AG's Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) related performance and governance, you can look at several key reports and disclosures:\n\n1. **Annual Report**: This document typically includes an overview of the company’s operations, financial performance, and strategic direction. It may also contain sections dedicated to sustainability or corporate responsibility that detail ESG initiatives and performance.\n\n2. **Sustainability Report**: Many companies publish standalone sustainability reports that focus specifically on their environmental impact, social contributions, and governance practices. These reports often include detailed metrics, targets, and progress updates.\n\n3. **Integrated Report**: Some companies combine financial and non-financial information in an integrated report, which can provide a comprehensive view of the company's strategy, governance, performance, and future prospects from an ESG perspective.\n\n4. **Corporate Responsibility Report**: Similar to a sustainability report, this document outlines the company’s efforts towards sustainable development and corporate citizenship.\n\n5. **Proxy Statement (Annual General Meeting Report)**: This document is required by regulatory bodies such as the German Federal Financial Supervisory Authority (BaFin) and provides information about the company’s governance structure, including board composition, executive compensation, and voting results from shareholder meetings.\n\n6. **CSR (Corporate Social Responsibility) Reports**: These reports highlight the company’s commitment to ethical business practices, community involvement, and social welfare programs.\n\n7. **Environmental Impact Statements**: If applicable, these documents detail the company’s environmental policies, emissions data, energy usage, and waste management practices.\n\n8. **Governance Documents**: These include codes of conduct, ethics policies, and compliance programs that outline how the company manages risks and ensures accountability.\n\n9. **External Ratings and Assessments**: Companies like MSCI, Sustainalytics, and others provide independent assessments of a company’s ESG performance. These ratings can be found on the respective rating agency websites.\n\nFor specific details regarding freenet AG, it would be best to visit their official website where they likely have downloadable versions of these reports available under the \"Investor Relations\" or \"Corporate Responsibility\" section. Additionally, platforms like Bloomberg, Refinitiv, and others may also host aggregated ESG data for freenet AG.",
