      "solution": "2023 annual base salary, bonuses, certification audit, job-related characteristics, professional position, qualification-related employee characteristics, seniority, skill level, tolerance threshold of 5%, work experience",
      "attempt": "I don't have specific information about the exact criteria that were evaluated during Uniper's 2023 audit for ensuring fair compensation practices. However, typically, when companies undergo audits related to fair compensation practices, several key areas are often examined:\n\n1. **Pay Equity**: This involves comparing salaries and benefits across different genders, races, and other protected classes to ensure there is no discrimination in pay.\n\n2. **Compliance with Legal Standards**: Auditors check if the company complies with local labor laws and regulations regarding minimum wage, overtime, and other employment standards.\n\n3. **Transparency in Compensation Policies**: The clarity and accessibility of the company’s compensation policies and procedures are reviewed to ensure they are understandable and applied consistently.\n\n4. **Performance-Based Pay**: Evaluating whether compensation is tied to performance metrics and how these metrics are defined and measured.\n\n5. **Market Comparisons**: Assessing how the company’s compensation packages compare to industry standards and competitors to ensure competitiveness and fairness.\n\n6. **Employee Feedback**: Gathering input from employees on their perceptions of the fairness of the compensation system can also be part of an audit process.\n\n7. **Review of Benefits and Perks**: Ensuring that non-monetary benefits (such as health insurance, retirement plans, vacation time) are distributed fairly and are competitive within the industry.\n\n8. **Documentation and Record-Keeping**: Checking that all compensation-related documents are properly maintained and accessible for review.\n\nFor precise details about Uniper's 2023 audit, you would need to refer to the company's official reports or contact Uniper directly for the most accurate and detailed information.",
