      "attempt": "UNIQA Group, an Austrian insurance company, focuses on several key markets across Europe. When it comes to the analysis of equal pay, the specific countries that are highlighted as core markets can vary based on the strategic focus and operational scope at different times. However, typically, such analyses would include countries where UNIQA has significant operations and a substantial workforce.\n\nFor equal pay analysis, UNIQA might consider its major European markets, which often include:\n\n1. Austria (where UNIQA is headquartered)\n2. Germany\n3. Italy\n4. Czech Republic\n5. Slovakia\n\nThese countries are among the most important for UNIQA's business activities, and conducting an equal pay analysis in these regions would help ensure fair compensation practices across its operations. It's important to note that the exact list of countries could change depending on UNIQA's current priorities and the specific scope of the equal pay initiative. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, it would be best to refer directly to UNIQA's official communications or reports.",
