      "attempt": "It seems there might be some confusion in your query as \"AMAG\" could refer to different organizations depending on the context. If you're referring to AMAG Pharmaceuticals, Inc., which is a pharmaceutical company based in the United States, they typically follow general corporate governance practices and may adhere to broader industry standards and regulations rather than having a widely publicized specific set of human rights and compliance policies that are unique to them.\n\nHowever, many companies, including pharmaceuticals, often base their human rights and compliance frameworks on international guidelines such as the United Nations Guiding Principles on Business and Human Rights (UNGPs) and the OECD Guidelines for Multinational Enterprises. Additionally, they would comply with local laws and regulations where they operate.\n\nIf AMAG Pharmaceuticals or another specific entity is what you're asking about, it would be best to look at their official website or annual reports for detailed information on their policies and frameworks. They usually outline their commitment to ethical business practices, human rights, and compliance in these documents.\n\nCould you please clarify which AMAG you are referring to, or provide more context so I can give a more accurate answer?",
