      "question": "Which factors determine rental pricing in Germany under the current housing framework?",
      "answer": "average rent including ancillary expenses, below 30% of the average disposable household income, binding, consensual process, negotiations between tenants' associations and landlords, price-controlled, prices are fixed, qualified rent indices, rents are generally set, statutory parameters, usual local rents",
      "type": "Factoid",
