      "problem": "Which personal attributes are safeguarded against discrimination under the company's ESG commitments?",
      "solution": "Age, Disability, Gender, Ideology, Nationalities, Origin, Personal characteristics, Religious affiliation, Sexual orientation, Skin color",
      "attempt": "Under most companies' Environmental, Social, and Governance (ESG) commitments, the social aspect often includes a strong focus on diversity, equity, and inclusion. This typically means that personal attributes such as race, gender, age, religion, disability status, sexual orientation, and other characteristics are safeguarded against discrimination. Companies usually commit to creating an inclusive workplace where all employees feel valued and respected regardless of these personal attributes.\n\nTo get specific details about which personal attributes are protected under a particular company’s ESG commitments, you would need to review their official ESG reports or policies directly. Each organization may have its own specific list based on local laws, industry standards, and corporate values.",
