      "solution": "Commerz Real, Commerzbank Aktiengesellschaft, IT, mBank, operations, sales and contracts units",
      "attempt": "To answer your question accurately, I'll need to clarify that you're referring to a specific context or document, as the involvement of organizations and units in implementing ESG (Environmental, Social, and Governance) related health and workplace initiatives can vary widely depending on the industry, company size, and geographical location.\n\nHowever, generally speaking, here are some common types of organizations and units that might be involved:\n\n1. **Corporate Social Responsibility (CSR) Departments**: These departments often lead the charge in developing and implementing ESG policies, including those related to health and safety in the workplace.\n\n2. **Health and Safety Units**: Within many companies, there are dedicated teams focused on ensuring the physical and mental well-being of employees. They work on creating safe working environments and promoting healthy lifestyles.\n\n3. **Human Resources (HR) Departments**: HR plays a crucial role in managing employee relations, benefits, and training programs that can contribute to better health outcomes and a more positive workplace culture.\n\n4. **Sustainability Teams**: In larger corporations, there may be a separate sustainability team that focuses on environmental and social issues, which can include workplace health initiatives.\n\n5. **External Consultants and Partners**: Companies often collaborate with external experts in health and safety, sustainability, and governance to develop and implement effective ESG strategies.\n\n6. **Government Agencies and Regulatory Bodies**: Depending on the country or region, government bodies may have regulations and guidelines that companies must follow regarding workplace health and safety.\n\n7. **Non-Governmental Organizations (NGOs)**: NGOs focused on health, labor rights, and environmental protection can provide guidance and support for companies looking to improve their ESG performance.\n\n8. **Employee Wellness Programs**: Often managed by HR or a dedicated wellness team, these programs aim to promote physical and mental health among employees.\n\nIf you could provide more specific details about the context you're referring to, I could give a more precise answer tailored to that situation.",
