      "attempt": "In Poland, as in many other countries, companies offer various health and wellness programs to support the well-being of their employees. These offerings can vary widely depending on the company's size, industry, and resources, but here are some common examples:\n\n1. **Health Insurance**: Many companies provide comprehensive health insurance plans that cover medical expenses, including preventive care, treatments, and sometimes even dental and vision care.\n\n2. **Employee Assistance Programs (EAP)**: These programs offer confidential counseling services for personal or work-related issues, such as stress management, family problems, or substance abuse.\n\n3. **Fitness Reimbursements**: Some employers reimburse employees for gym memberships or fitness classes, encouraging regular physical activity.\n\n4. **Wellness Programs**: Companies may organize workshops, seminars, or online courses focused on topics like nutrition, mental health, stress management, and healthy lifestyle choices.\n\n5. **Flexible Work Arrangements**: Offering flexible working hours, remote work options, or job sharing can help reduce stress and improve work-life balance.\n\n6. **On-Site Facilities**: Larger companies might have on-site gyms, meditation rooms, or quiet spaces where employees can relax and recharge during breaks.\n\n7. **Subsidized Healthy Food Options**: Providing access to healthy food options in cafeterias or subsidizing healthy meal deliveries can promote better eating habits.\n\n8. **Mental Health Support**: This includes access to mental health professionals, mindfulness training, and stress management workshops.\n\n9. **Annual Health Check-ups**: Some companies arrange for annual health check-ups to ensure early detection and prevention of illnesses.\n\n10. **Parental Leave and Childcare Support**: Offering generous parental leave policies and possibly supporting childcare costs can help employees manage family responsibilities more effectively.\n\nThese offerings reflect a growing trend towards holistic employee well-being, recognizing that healthier, happier employees tend to be more productive and engaged at work. It's worth noting that specific benefits can vary significantly between different companies and industries within Poland.",
      "grading": "No"
    },
