      "question": "Why were energy-saving measures, site closures, and relocations critical in reducing indirect emissions from electricity purchases (Scope 2.1), and how do these actions align with TAKKT's broader ESG strategy?",
      "answer": "Indirect emissions from electricity purchases (Scope 2.1) were reduced by 306 t CO₂e, a 7 percent decrease. This reduction was primarily driven by energy-saving measures, site closures, and relocations to more energy-efficient premises.",
