      "question": "Why does the Supervisory Board prioritize qualifications over gender in its approach to Board of Management appointments, and how does this align with broader ESG principles of governance and diversity?",
      "answer": "The Supervisory Board does not view gender as a qualification that inherently makes a candidate suitable for a position. Instead, it emphasizes personal and professional qualifications as the primary criteria.",
