      "question": "Why was the previous upper limit for severance payments in the event of a change of control structured as three times the annual remuneration, and how does its cancellation reflect evolving governance priorities?",
      "answer": "The previous upper limit for severance payments in the event of a change of control was set at three times the total annual remuneration of the Chairman of the Management Board. This provision was later cancelled with effect from 1 January 2024.",
