        "paragraph": "In the event that an Executive Board member becomes permanently incapable of working, the defined benefit pension agreements for Executive Board members provide for a transitional payment. The amount of this payment corresponds to the target amount of performance-based remuneration (Performance Bonus and Performance Shares) in the year in which the event triggering the benefits occurs. It is paid out in two tranches in the two following years. If an Executive Board member dies, their spouse receives 60 per cent of the transitional payment.\nThe pensionable income and the present value of the pension commitments as at 31 December 2023 are shown in the following tables in consolidated form for each Executive Board member:",
