      "solution": "Amended Climate Delegated Act (EU) 2023/2485, Appendix C of Annex 1, Delegated Act (EU) 2021/2139, current European legislation on chemicals",
      "attempt": "The DNSH criteria, which stands for \"Darkening of Natural Stone,\" is not a widely recognized term in the context of EU legislation on pollution prevention and control. However, it seems you might be referring to the Best Available Techniques (BAT) conclusions that are part of the Industrial Emissions Directive (IED), which is the main piece of EU legislation dealing with pollution prevention and control.\n\nThe Industrial Emissions Directive (Directive 2010/75/EU) integrates several previous directives related to large industrial installations and aims to prevent or reduce emissions to air, water, and land. The BAT conclusions under this directive provide guidance on how to achieve high environmental standards through the application of best available techniques.\n\nIf you're looking for specific criteria related to pollution prevention and control, the following EU legislative acts are key:\n\n1. **Industrial Emissions Directive (IED) (2010/75/EU)**: This directive sets out the requirements for integrated permits for industrial activities and includes provisions for the application of BAT conclusions.\n\n2. **Best Available Techniques Reference Documents (BREFs)**: These documents are developed by the European IPPC Bureau (EIIB) and provide detailed information on BAT for different industrial sectors. They are used to support the development of BAT conclusions under the IED.\n\nIf you meant to ask about a specific set of criteria or if there's another term you were thinking of, please clarify, and I can provide more targeted information.",
