      "attempt": "The analysis of compliance with EU Taxonomy criteria typically focuses on companies and production sites within the European Union, as the EU Taxonomy is a classification system developed by the European Commission to support the transition to a sustainable economy. However, given the global nature of many businesses, companies from various regions and countries outside the EU may also be analyzed for their alignment with these criteria.\n\nFor instance, multinational corporations (MNCs) with operations in different parts of the world might have their production sites assessed against the EU Taxonomy criteria as part of broader sustainability reporting or due to investor interest in understanding their environmental impact. Such assessments could include production sites located in North America, Asia, Africa, and other regions.\n\nWithout specific details about which study or report you're referring to, it's challenging to pinpoint exactly which regions and countries were analyzed. If you have a particular report or study in mind, providing more context would help in giving a more accurate answer.",
