      "attempt": "It seems there might be some confusion in your question. \"INDUS\" is not a recognized entity that applies directives under the EU Taxonomy framework. The EU Taxonomy is a classification system developed by the European Union to help companies and investors identify which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable. It is part of the broader Sustainable Finance Disclosure Regulation (SFDR) and the Non-Financial Reporting Directive (NFRD).\n\nIf you're referring to specific companies or organizations operating within the EU that are applying the EU Taxonomy for their 2023 financial year, it would be more accurate to mention the name of the company or organization. Each company that falls under the scope of the SFDR and NFRD must disclose how their activities align with the EU Taxonomy criteria.\n\nFor detailed information on how specific entities are applying the EU Taxonomy, you should refer to their sustainability reports or financial disclosures for the 2023 financial year. If you have a particular company or sector in mind, please provide more details so I can give you a more precise answer.",
