      "question_id": "validation:000771:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "difficulty_id": "F-000011",
      "id": "validation:000771:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "problem": "Which delegated regulations establish the framework and criteria for sustainable economic activities under the EU Taxonomy?",
      "solution": "Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2139, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2178, Delegated Regulation (EU) 2023/2486, Environmental Delegated Act, Regulation (EU) 2020/852",
      "attempt": "The framework and criteria for sustainable economic activities under the EU Taxonomy are established through a series of delegated acts adopted by the European Commission based on the initial regulation (EU) 2020/852, also known as the Taxonomy Regulation. These delegated acts provide detailed technical screening criteria that define what qualifies as an environmentally sustainable activity in terms of climate change mitigation and adaptation.\n\nSpecifically, the following delegated acts have been adopted:\n\n1. **Delegated Act (EU) 2021/337**: This act sets out the technical screening criteria for determining which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable in relation to climate change mitigation. It was published in February 2021 and entered into force on July 1, 2021.\n\n2. **Delegated Act (EU) 2021/2177**: This act provides the technical screening criteria for climate change adaptation activities. It was adopted in December 2021 and entered into force on January 1, 2022.\n\n3. **Delegated Act (EU) 2022/1296**: This act introduces additional details and clarifications to the existing criteria for climate change mitigation and adaptation, as well as new criteria for two environmental objectives: sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources; and transition to a circular economy. It was adopted in September 2022 and entered into force on January 1, 2023.\n\nThese delegated acts are crucial for providing clarity and consistency across the EU regarding what constitutes sustainable economic activities, thereby facilitating investment in green projects and helping companies to align their operations with sustainability goals.",
