      "id": "train:006108:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "problem": "What are the Delegated Regulations assessed by TeamViewer Group for EU Taxonomy compliance?",
      "solution": "Delegated Regulation 2021/2139, Delegated Regulation 2022/1214, Delegated Regulation 2023/2485, Delegated Regulation 2023/2486",
      "attempt": "TeamViewer Group, like many other companies, would assess various regulations and guidelines to ensure compliance with the EU Taxonomy for sustainable activities. The EU Taxonomy is a classification system that aims to provide a common language for investors and companies to understand which economic activities can be considered environmentally sustainable.\n\nThe Delegated Act (Regulation) referred to in the context of the EU Taxonomy is specifically the Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/297, which sets out the technical screening criteria for determining whether an economic activity qualifies as environmentally sustainable under the EU Taxonomy Regulation (Regulation (EU) 2020/852). This regulation covers six environmental objectives:\n\n1. Climate change mitigation.\n2. Climate change adaptation.\n3. Sustainable use and protection of water and marine resources.\n4. Transition to a circular economy.\n5. Pollution prevention and control.\n6. Protection and restoration of biodiversity and ecosystems.\n\nFor TeamViewer Group or any company to comply with these regulations, they would need to assess their activities against these criteria to determine if they contribute substantially to one or more of these environmental objectives without causing significant harm to the others. Compliance involves detailed analysis and reporting on how their operations align with the taxonomy's requirements.\n\nIt's important to note that while TeamViewer Group might have specific internal processes and assessments related to the EU Taxonomy, the actual regulatory framework is set by the European Commission through the aforementioned Delegated Regulation. Companies must then interpret and apply these regulations to their own business contexts.",
