      "question": "How does the 'do no significant harm' (DNSH) criterion influence the assessment of economic activities under the EU Taxonomy Regulation, and why did Zalando conclude that recent amendments did not affect its operations?",
      "answer": "The 'do no significant harm' (DNSH) criterion is part of the technical screening criteria under the EU Taxonomy Regulation. Zalando assessed these criteria in relation to Annex I and Annex II amendments but determined that the changes did not affect its activities.",
