      "question": "Why were leased hybrid and electric company cars classified as taxonomy-eligible rather than taxonomy-aligned in POLYTEC's assessment, and how does this reflect the EU Taxonomy's climate protection criteria?",
      "answer": "The focus of the taxonomy-eligible leasing costs assessment was on the costs of leased hybrid and electric company cars. These costs were allocated to economic sector 6.3, which includes local and regional passenger transport, but were only identified as taxonomy-eligible due to the limited climate protection contributions of hybrid vehicles.",
