      "question": "How do the DNSH criteria under the EU Taxonomy regulate the exclusion of specific hazardous substances in the manufacture of renewable energy technologies, and why is this significant for environmental sustainability?",
      "answer": "The DNSH criteria exclude the use of substances that deplete the ozone layer, mercury and mercury compounds, and persistent organic pollutants under the Stockholm Convention in the manufacture of renewable energy technologies.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
      "tag": "EU Taxonomy",
      "question_id": "train:006324:qa_pairs_non_factoid:0003",
      "difficulty_question_word": "why",
      "question_word_f1": 0.665,
