      "question": "Why is it important to distinguish between 'Taxonomy-eligible' and 'Taxonomy-aligned' activities in the EU Taxonomy framework, and how does this distinction affect regulatory compliance and investment decisions?",
      "answer": "In the context, 'Taxonomy-eligible' refers to activities that qualify under the EU Taxonomy framework, while 'Taxonomy-aligned' specifies that the eligible activity also meets the relevant environmental objective.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
