      "question": "Why is it important to include operating expenditures for planned investments in the OpEx calculation, and how does this support the expansion of taxonomy-aligned activities under EU Taxonomy principles?",
      "answer": "Operating expenditures for planned investments must be included in the OpEx calculation to account for costs associated with expanding taxonomy-aligned economic activities, such as workforce training and research and development.",
      "type": "Descriptive, non-factoid",
