      "question": "Why is it necessary to include specific operating expenses, such as non-capitalized R&D costs, short-term leases, and maintenance and repairs of fixed assets, in the denominator for the Opex-KPI calculation under the EU Taxonomy framework?",
      "answer": "The denominator for determining the Opex-KPI must include operating expenses related to non-capitalized research and development costs, short-term leases, and maintenance and repairs of fixed assets. These expenses must be directly or indirectly allocable to taxonomy-aligned activities.",
