        "paragraph": "Bechtle's EU Taxonomy disclosures detail capital expenditures (CapEx) for taxonomy-eligible and aligned activities across its mobility and property segments from 2021 to 2023. For 2023, Bechtle reported €120,448k in total Taxonomy-eligible CapEx, of which €52,408k was Taxonomy-aligned. This represents 48.1% and 20.9% respectively of the total CapEx of €250,400k, which excludes construction in progress (CIP) and planned down payments. Key contributing eligible activities for 2023 included €37,477k for automobiles and lorries (€14,619k aligned), €476k for energy-efficient equipment (all aligned), €1,923k for charging stations (all aligned), and €80,572k for buildings (€35,390k aligned). In 2022, total Taxonomy-eligible CapEx was €64,264k, with €20,402k aligned, from a total CapEx of €147,700k, yielding 43.5% eligible and 13.8% aligned shares. Specifically, for 'Renewable energies' (7.6), €86k in both eligible and aligned CapEx was reported in 2022, while no CapEx was recorded for this activity in 2021 or 2023. For 2021, €56,876k was identified as eligible CapEx out of a total CapEx of €104,400k, resulting in a 54.5% eligibility share; however, taxonomy alignment was not assessed for this period. Activities such as renovation of existing buildings and total energy efficiency of buildings consistently reported no CapEx across the presented years. It is noted that operational expenditures (OpEx) for activities 5.1, 7.2 to 7.7, and 8.1 are not reported, as they fall below the 1% disclosure threshold. Furthermore, CapEx figures since 2022 exclude CIP and down payments, as these are only considered upon building completion for alignment assessment, and rent increases and contract extensions were not checked for alignment in 2022 and 2023.",
