        "table_caption": "Proportion of CapEx / Total CapEx",
        "paragraph": "The Amadeus Fire Group's capital expenditure (CapEx) disclosures for the 2023 financial year, as defined by Delegated Regulation (EU) 2021/2178, present the proportions of Taxonomy-eligible and Taxonomy-aligned CapEx across the six environmental objectives. A substantial 70.98% of total CapEx was identified as Taxonomy-eligible, exclusively contributing to the Climate Change Mitigation (CCM) objective. Conversely, no CapEx was found eligible for Climate Change Adaptation (CCA), Sustainable Use and Protection of Water and Marine Resources (WTR), Transition to a Circular Economy (CE), Pollution Prevention and Control (PPC), or Protection and Restoration of Biodiversity and Ecosystems (BIO). The proportion of Taxonomy-aligned CapEx stands at a mere 0.05%, solely under the Climate Change Mitigation objective. This alignment stems from specific additions to right-of-use assets for leased vehicles, where one vehicle out of the ten identified met all technical screening criteria for substantial contribution and the Do No Significant Harm (DNSH) criteria. It is important to note that while other Taxonomy-eligible items, such as additions to right-of-use assets for leased bikes, met technical screening criteria for climate change mitigation, they did not achieve full alignment in 2023 due to unconfirmed compliance with minimum social safeguards.",
