      "id": "train:001904:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "problem": "Which STEM competitions and events in Germany contribute to fostering sustainable scientific education?",
      "solution": "Chemie, die stimmt, Erfinderlabor, Hesse/Thuringia state seminar, Jugend forscht, STEM competitions, Tag der Mathematik, international biology and chemistry Olympiads",
      "attempt": "Germany hosts several STEM (Science, Technology, Engineering, and Mathematics) competitions and events that contribute to fostering sustainable scientific education. These initiatives not only encourage students to engage with STEM subjects but also promote sustainability and innovation. Here are some notable examples:\n\n1. **Jugend forscht (Youth Research)**: This is one of the largest youth research competitions in Europe, where young people from all over Germany present their own research projects. The competition covers various fields including environmental science, which often includes projects related to sustainability.\n\n2. **Deutsche Jugend forscht (German Youth Research)**: Similar to Jugend forscht, this competition focuses on promoting scientific research among young people. It encourages projects that address real-world problems, including those related to sustainability.\n\n3. **Eco-Schools Programme**: While not a competition per se, this program is part of the international Foundation for Environmental Education (FEE) network. It aims to integrate sustainable development into school curricula and daily school life. Schools can participate in various activities and projects focused on environmental issues.\n\n4. **Bundeswettbewerb Chemie (Federal Chemistry Competition)**: This competition challenges students to solve chemistry-related problems, often including topics related to sustainable chemistry and environmental protection.\n\n5. **Technikum der Zukunft (Future Technical Institute)**: This event is designed to inspire young people's interest in technology and engineering. It includes workshops, lectures, and competitions that often touch upon sustainable technologies and practices.\n\n6. **Deutscher Physik-Wettbewerb (German Physics Competition)**: This competition encourages students to explore physics problems, sometimes including those related to renewable energy and sustainable technologies.\n\n7. **Innovationen für die Energiewende (Innovations for the Energy Transition)**: This is an initiative that supports young innovators working on solutions for the energy transition, focusing on renewable energy sources and sustainable energy use.\n\n8. **Jugend hackt (Youth hacks)**: This series of hackathons encourages young people to develop innovative solutions using digital technologies. Many participants focus on creating applications or systems that promote sustainability and environmental awareness.\n\nThese events and competitions play a crucial role in nurturing a generation of scientifically literate individuals who are aware of and committed to addressing global sustainability challenges. They provide platforms for students to apply theoretical knowledge in practical scenarios, fostering creativity, problem-solving skills, and a sense of responsibility towards the environment.",
