      "problem": "Which activities are examples of Scope 3 emissions according to MTU's sustainability strategy?",
      "solution": "downstream use of products, emissions relating to capital expenditure, evaluate MTU's Scope 3 emissions, upstream and downstream activities, upstream value creation by suppliers",
      "attempt": "MTU Aero Engines, a leading manufacturer of commercial and military aircraft engines, has a comprehensive sustainability strategy that includes the reduction of greenhouse gas emissions across its value chain. According to this strategy, Scope 3 emissions refer to all indirect emissions that occur in a company’s value chain and not directly from its own operations or the generation of electricity.\n\nExamples of activities that fall under Scope 3 emissions for MTU include:\n\n1. **Purchased Goods and Services**: Emissions related to the production of goods and services purchased by MTU.\n2. **Upstream Transportation and Distribution**: Emissions from transporting raw materials and components to MTU’s facilities and distributing finished products.\n3. **Waste Generated in Operations**: Emissions associated with waste disposal and treatment processes.\n4. **Business Travel**: Emissions from flights, road trips, and other forms of travel undertaken by employees for business purposes.\n5. **Employee Commuting**: Emissions from employees commuting to and from work.\n6. **Use of Sold Products**: For MTU, this would include emissions from the operation of the engines they produce over their lifecycle.\n7. **End-of-Life Treatment of Sold Products**: Emissions related to the disposal or recycling of engines at the end of their service life.\n8. **Leased Assets**: Emissions from assets leased by MTU.\n9. **Investments**: Emissions related to investments made by MTU.\n10. **Franchises and Joint Ventures**: Emissions from joint ventures and franchises in which MTU is involved.\n\nMTU aims to reduce these emissions through various strategies, including optimizing supply chains, promoting sustainable practices among suppliers, and developing more fuel-efficient engine technologies. By addressing these Scope 3 emissions, MTU seeks to minimize its environmental impact throughout its entire value chain.",
