      "solution": "business travel, downstream logistics, employee commuting, mobile combustion, purchased heat, purchased working materials",
      "attempt": "Manz AG, like many other companies, reports its greenhouse gas (GHG) emissions according to the Greenhouse Gas Protocol, which categorizes emissions into three scopes: Scope 1, Scope 2, and Scope 3. Scope 3 emissions encompass all indirect emissions that occur in a company’s value chain outside of its direct operations.\n\nFor Manz AG, Scope 3 emissions would include a wide range of activities related to its supply chain and downstream use of its products. These can generally be broken down into several categories:\n\n1. **Upstream Activities**: This includes emissions from purchased goods and services, capital goods, fuel and energy-related activities not included in Scope 2, waste generated in operations, and business travel.\n   \n2. **Downstream Activities**: This involves emissions from the use of sold products, leased assets, and the end-of-life treatment of sold products.\n\n3. **Other Activities**: This category may include emissions from transportation and distribution, outsourced operations, and investments.\n\nTo get specific details on how Manz AG categorizes and measures its Scope 3 emissions, you would need to refer to their latest sustainability report or GHG inventory report. Companies often provide detailed breakdowns of these emissions in their annual reports or dedicated sustainability sections of their websites.",
