        "paragraph": "Operating our vessels is associated with specific health and safety risks for our employees. These include hazards posed by large, heavy, moving equipment, stress caused by noise, travel through different time and climate zones, the motion of the vessel and bad weather. NfR\nImproving safety on board is a top priority for us. That is why we are permanently working on safety, with regular training courses on safety-relevant topics for marine personnel forming a key cornerstone of our efforts. NfR\n<sup>4</sup> The individual data on deficiency rates for the charter fleet are not recorded centrally; two bareboat charter vessels included\n- 04 **FOREWORD OF THE EXECUTIVE BOARD**\n- **ABOUT THIS REPORT** 06\n- **HAPAG-LLOYD**  $10<sub>1</sub>$\n- **44 SUSTAINABILITY AT HAPAG-LLOYD**\n- 69 CLIMATE AND **ENVIRONMENTAL PROTECTION**\n- 85 EMPLOYEES",
