      "problem": "What reporting elements are used by Evonik to map its contributions to the Sustainable Development Goals?",
      "solution": "GRI content index, SDG index, Sustainability Focus Areas, p. 140, p. 153",
      "attempt": "Evonik, a global leader in specialty chemicals, aligns its sustainability efforts with the United Nations' Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs). To map its contributions to these goals, Evonik uses several key reporting elements that help in transparently communicating its impact and progress. Here are some of the main elements:\n\n1. **Sustainability Report**: Evonik publishes an annual Sustainability Report which details how the company is contributing to the SDGs. This report includes quantitative data and qualitative information on various aspects such as environmental performance, social responsibility, and economic contributions.\n\n2. **Materiality Analysis**: The company conducts a materiality analysis to identify the most significant sustainability topics for its business and stakeholders. This helps in focusing its efforts on areas where it can make the greatest impact towards the SDGs.\n\n3. **Stakeholder Engagement**: Engaging with stakeholders, including customers, employees, investors, and NGOs, helps Evonik understand the expectations and needs related to the SDGs. This engagement process informs the company's strategy and reporting.\n\n4. **KPIs and Metrics**: Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) are established to measure progress against specific SDGs. These metrics cover a range of areas from reducing greenhouse gas emissions to improving product safety and enhancing employee development programs.\n\n5. **Case Studies and Examples**: Specific examples and case studies are provided in the reports to illustrate how Evonik’s products and services contribute to achieving the SDGs. For instance, innovations in renewable energy solutions or advancements in healthcare materials.\n\n6. **Integration into Business Strategy**: Evonik integrates the SDGs into its overall business strategy, ensuring that sustainability considerations are part of decision-making processes across all levels of the organization.\n\n7. **External Verification**: To ensure transparency and credibility, parts of Evonik’s sustainability reporting may be externally verified or audited.\n\n8. **Online Platforms and Dashboards**: Utilizing digital platforms and dashboards to provide real-time updates and interactive tools for stakeholders to explore Evonik’s contributions to the SDGs.\n\nBy using these elements, Evonik not only tracks its progress but also communicates effectively with its stakeholders about its commitment to sustainable development.",
