      "solution": "ISO 14001, ISO 45001, ISO 9001, ISO certifications, environmental management systems, occupational health and safety management systems",
      "attempt": "The ANDRITZ GROUP, a global market leader in plant engineering for the pulp and paper, hydropower production, metals and mining, and other industries, ensures compliance with sustainability-related management systems through various certifications. While specific to ANDRITZ, common certifications that align with sustainability and environmental management include:\n\n1. **ISO 14001**: This is an international standard for Environmental Management Systems (EMS). It helps organizations minimize how their operations negatively affect the environment, comply with applicable laws, regulations, and other environmentally oriented requirements, and continually improve their environmental performance.\n\n2. **ISO 50001**: This standard focuses on energy management systems. It provides a framework to help organizations implement the necessary processes and best practices to improve energy efficiency, reduce energy consumption, and decrease greenhouse gas emissions.\n\n3. **ISO 9001**: Although primarily focused on quality management, ISO 9001 can also contribute to sustainability goals by ensuring consistent quality in products and services, which can lead to reduced waste and improved resource efficiency.\n\n4. **Other Certifications**: Depending on the specific industry and region, ANDRITZ might also pursue sector-specific certifications or regional standards that address sustainability concerns. For example, in hydropower, they might adhere to guidelines set by the International Hydropower Association (IHA) Sustainability Assessment Protocol.\n\nANDRITZ GROUP's commitment to sustainability is reflected not only in these certifications but also in its broader corporate social responsibility (CSR) initiatives and policies aimed at sustainable development and environmental stewardship. To get the most accurate and up-to-date information regarding ANDRITZ GROUP's specific certifications and sustainability efforts, it would be advisable to consult their official website or contact their corporate communications department directly.",
