      "question": "Which sustainability-related metrics are included in Vonovia's SPI framework to measure corporate performance?",
      "answer": "CO<sub>2</sub> intensity of our housing stock, Energy efficiency of new buildings, Increased customer satisfaction, Increased employee satisfaction, proportion of accessible (partially) modernized newly let apartments, proportion of women in top management",
      "type": "Factoid",
      "tag": "Sustainability",
      "question_id": "train:000266:qa_pairs_factoid:0002",
      "difficulty_id": "F-000014",
      "id": "train:000266:qa_pairs_factoid:0002",
      "problem": "Which sustainability-related metrics are included in Vonovia's SPI framework to measure corporate performance?",
      "solution": "CO<sub>2</sub> intensity of our housing stock, Energy efficiency of new buildings, Increased customer satisfaction, Increased employee satisfaction, proportion of accessible (partially) modernized newly let apartments, proportion of women in top management",
      "attempt": "Vonovia, one of the largest owner-operators of residential properties in Europe, incorporates several sustainability-related metrics into its Sustainability Performance Indicator (SPI) framework to measure corporate performance. These metrics are designed to reflect the company’s commitment to environmental, social, and governance (ESG) standards. Here are some key sustainability-related metrics included in Vonovia's SPI framework:\n\n1. **Energy Efficiency**: This includes indicators such as the energy consumption per square meter of living space, the share of renewable energy used, and the progress towards achieving energy efficiency targets.\n\n2. **Emissions**: Metrics related to greenhouse gas emissions, including CO2 emissions from heating, electricity use, and other sources. Vonovia also tracks the reduction in emissions over time.\n\n3. **Water Management**: Indicators for water consumption and efforts to reduce water usage through efficient technologies and practices.\n\n4. **Waste Management**: Metrics on waste production, recycling rates, and initiatives to minimize waste generation.\n\n5. **Sustainable Building Practices**: This covers the percentage of new buildings that meet certain sustainability standards (e.g., LEED, DGNB), as well as the renovation of existing buildings to improve their sustainability.\n\n6. **Social Responsibility**: Includes measures related to tenant satisfaction, diversity and inclusion within the workforce, and community engagement activities.\n\n7. **Health and Safety**: Indicators for workplace safety, accident rates, and health programs for employees.\n\n8. **Corporate Governance**: Metrics related to transparency, compliance with regulations, and ethical business practices.\n\n9. **Innovation and Technology**: Measures the adoption of innovative solutions aimed at improving sustainability, such as smart home technology and digitalization efforts.\n\nThese metrics help Vonovia not only to track its progress towards sustainability goals but also to align with broader industry trends and regulatory requirements. The company regularly publishes reports detailing its performance against these SPIs, providing stakeholders with transparent information about its sustainability efforts.",
