      "problem": "Who are the sustainability-focused organizations PORR collaborates with or exchanges expertise?",
      "solution": "Bienenlieb, Deutsche Gesellschaft für nachhaltiges Bauen (DGNB), Gesellschaft für Ökologie und Abfallwirtschaft, Umweltausschuss der Deutschen Bauindustrie, Umweltbundesamt, Umweltdachverhand, Umweltschutzverband, Österreichische Gesellschaft für Nachhaltige Immobilienwirtschaft (ÖGNI)",
      "attempt": "PORR, an Austrian construction company, is known for its commitment to sustainability and innovation in the construction industry. While specific collaborations can vary over time, PORR often works with various organizations that share its vision of sustainable development. Some of these include:\n\n1. **European Construction Industry Federation (FIEC)**: PORR participates in FIEC initiatives aimed at promoting sustainable construction practices across Europe.\n\n2. **World Business Council for Sustainable Development (WBCSD)**: This organization brings together leading companies from around the world to accelerate change towards sustainable development. PORR may engage with WBCSD to exchange best practices and innovative solutions.\n\n3. **DGNB (Deutsche Gesellschaft für Nachhaltiges Bauen)**: The German Sustainable Building Council promotes sustainable building practices and certifies buildings based on their environmental impact. PORR might collaborate with DGNB on projects that aim for high sustainability standards.\n\n4. **Green Building Councils**: In various countries, Green Building Councils promote sustainable building practices. PORR could be involved in local Green Building Councils in regions where it operates, such as the Austrian Green Building Council (ÖGNI).\n\n5. **Research Institutions and Universities**: PORR collaborates with academic institutions to advance research in sustainable construction materials, energy-efficient designs, and other areas crucial for reducing the environmental footprint of buildings.\n\n6. **Local Government Agencies**: Depending on the location of its projects, PORR may work closely with local government bodies that have sustainability mandates or initiatives.\n\n7. **NGOs and Environmental Groups**: Organizations focused on environmental protection and sustainability advocacy can also be partners in promoting sustainable construction practices.\n\nIt's important to note that direct partnerships and collaborations can evolve, and the specifics of these relationships might change over time. For the most current information, it would be advisable to consult PORR’s official communications or contact them directly.",
