      "problem": "Which entities and initiatives are involved in monitoring and addressing the sustainability of mobile network technologies?",
      "solution": "1&1, Bundesamt für Strahlenschutz, Deutschland spricht über 5G, Federal Government, Federal Office for Radiation Protection",
      "attempt": "Monitoring and addressing the sustainability of mobile network technologies involves a variety of entities and initiatives from both the public and private sectors. Here are some key players:\n\n1. **International Telecommunication Union (ITU)**: The ITU is a specialized agency of the United Nations that coordinates telecommunications operations and services throughout the world. It plays a significant role in setting standards for sustainable development in telecommunication technologies.\n\n2. **GSMA**: The GSMA represents the interests of mobile operators worldwide, and it works to ensure that mobile technology and services benefit people everywhere. It has several initiatives focused on sustainability, including efforts to reduce the environmental impact of mobile networks.\n\n3. **GreenTouch Consortium**: This is a global, industry-driven consortium that aims to develop and promote energy-efficient technologies for communication networks. Its work includes research and development aimed at reducing the carbon footprint of mobile networks.\n\n4. **European Telecommunications Standards Institute (ETSI)**: ETSI develops standards for information and communication technologies (ICTs) across Europe and globally. It has initiatives related to green ICT, which include guidelines and standards for more sustainable mobile network technologies.\n\n5. **Mobile Ecosystem Forum (MEF)**: MEF focuses on driving collaboration within the mobile ecosystem to address challenges such as sustainability. They work with operators, vendors, and other stakeholders to promote sustainable practices.\n\n6. **Environmental NGOs**: Organizations like Greenpeace and the World Wide Fund for Nature (WWF) also play roles in advocating for more sustainable practices in the ICT sector, including mobile networks. They often conduct research, publish reports, and engage in campaigns to raise awareness about environmental issues related to technology.\n\n7. **National Regulatory Bodies**: In many countries, there are regulatory bodies responsible for overseeing telecommunications. These bodies often have policies and guidelines aimed at promoting sustainability within the mobile network sector.\n\n8. **Telecommunications Companies**: Major telecom companies themselves are increasingly focusing on sustainability. For example, they may set targets for reducing energy consumption, increasing the use of renewable energy sources, and improving the recyclability of their products.\n\n9. **Research Institutions and Universities**: Many academic institutions conduct research into sustainable technologies and practices for mobile networks. This can include everything from developing new materials for hardware to creating more efficient software algorithms.\n\nThese entities and initiatives work together through various partnerships, collaborations, and standard-setting processes to monitor and improve the sustainability of mobile network technologies.",
