      "solution": "Asia, India, Latin America, North Africa, North America, North Europe, South Europe, the Middle East",
      "attempt": "Hapag-Lloyd is one of the world's leading liner shipping companies, operating a comprehensive network that spans all major trade routes. To support its global terminal and logistics sustainability goals, Hapag-Lloyd operates in numerous regions around the world. Here are some key areas where it focuses its efforts:\n\n1. **Europe**: Hapag-Lloyd has a significant presence in European ports, including Hamburg (where it is headquartered), Antwerp, Rotterdam, and many others. It aims to reduce emissions and improve efficiency through sustainable practices.\n\n2. **Asia**: The company operates extensively across Asia, with key terminals in China, Singapore, India, and other countries. Initiatives include investments in cleaner technologies and sustainable port operations.\n\n3. **North America**: Hapag-Lloyd serves North American ports such as Los Angeles, Long Beach, New York/New Jersey, and others. Sustainability efforts here focus on reducing carbon footprints and enhancing supply chain resilience.\n\n4. **Latin America**: Operations extend into South American ports like Santos, Buenos Aires, and Cartagena, with a focus on sustainable logistics solutions tailored to regional needs.\n\n5. **Middle East and Africa**: Hapag-Lloyd also operates in various Middle Eastern and African ports, promoting sustainable practices and supporting local economies while minimizing environmental impact.\n\n6. **Oceania**: In regions like Australia and New Zealand, Hapag-Lloyd works towards sustainable shipping and logistics solutions that cater to the unique challenges and opportunities of these areas.\n\nHapag-Lloyd’s sustainability initiatives often involve partnerships with local authorities, terminal operators, and other stakeholders to implement green technologies, optimize routes for fuel efficiency, and promote circular economy principles within the maritime industry. These efforts are part of a broader strategy to meet international sustainability standards and contribute positively to global environmental goals.",
