      "problem": "Which products developed by Evonik contribute to reducing environmental impacts?",
      "solution": "Excel® Rejuvenation process, POLYVEST® for tires with lower rolling resistance, TEGO® RC silicones, additives for hydraulic fluids, amino acids for animal nutrition, metal oxides for lithium-ion batteries, silica in paper production, silica-based rheology modifier",
      "attempt": "Evonik Industries is a global leader in specialty chemicals and has developed several products aimed at reducing environmental impacts. Here are some examples of their contributions:\n\n1. **AQUACOAT®**: This is a water-based acrylic polymer used in coatings that can help reduce volatile organic compounds (VOCs) emissions compared to solvent-based systems. It's used in various applications such as wood coatings, architectural paints, and industrial maintenance coatings.\n\n2. **VESTAMIN®**: These polyamines are used in epoxy resins for coatings and adhesives. They can improve the performance of these materials while also contributing to more sustainable manufacturing processes due to their lower toxicity and reduced environmental impact compared to traditional curing agents.\n\n3. **VINNOL E**: This is an alkyd resin used in waterborne coatings. It helps in reducing the use of solvents and thus lowers the environmental footprint of coating formulations.\n\n4. **Tego® Surfactants**: These surfactants are designed to enhance the efficiency of cleaning products, thereby reducing the amount of product needed and lowering the environmental impact of cleaning processes.\n\n5. **CAB-O-SIL® and CAB-O-SPERSE®**: These are fumed silica products used in various industries including paints, inks, and adhesives. They can improve the rheology of formulations, leading to better performance with less material usage, which can reduce waste and energy consumption.\n\n6. **EVEOX™**: This is a range of bio-based polyols derived from renewable resources, which can be used in the production of polyurethane foams. By using renewable feedstocks, these products help reduce dependency on fossil fuels and lower greenhouse gas emissions.\n\n7. **SILIKOPUR®**: This is a silicone oil used in various applications, including lubricants and release agents. Its high performance allows for efficient use, reducing waste and improving sustainability in manufacturing processes.\n\nThese products demonstrate Evonik's commitment to developing innovative solutions that not only meet customer needs but also support environmental sustainability.",
