      "problem": "Which technologies are employed by Vossloh to sustainably mitigate noise in railbound traffic?",
      "solution": "cellentic components, grinding, improving rail acoustics, less than 78 dB(A), milling machine VTM compact, noise reduction of up to 10 dB(A), rail fastening systems with a high plastic content, rail machining technologies, reducing noise in railbound traffic, structure-borne noise, whisper switches",
      "attempt": "Vossloh, a leading company in the railway industry, employs several advanced technologies to reduce noise in rail-bound traffic, contributing to a more sustainable and quieter environment. Here are some of the key technologies and approaches:\n\n1. **Quiet Wheel Technology**: Vossloh develops wheels that are designed to minimize noise during operation. This includes optimizing wheel profiles and materials to reduce the impact noise and rolling noise.\n\n2. **Low-Noise Track Components**: By using quieter track components such as rubber pads under the rails or special types of ballast, Vossloh helps to absorb vibrations and reduce noise transmission from the tracks to the surrounding environment.\n\n3. **Advanced Rail Grinding Techniques**: Regular grinding of the rail surface can help maintain a smooth profile, which reduces noise caused by irregularities on the rail surface. Vossloh uses sophisticated grinding machines and techniques to achieve this.\n\n4. **Innovative Fastening Systems**: Special fastening systems are used to secure the rails to the sleepers. These systems are designed to dampen vibrations and reduce the transmission of noise from the track to the ground.\n\n5. **Use of Composite Materials**: In some applications, Vossloh incorporates composite materials into their products, which can be lighter and quieter than traditional steel components, thereby reducing overall noise levels.\n\n6. **Integrated Noise Management Solutions**: Beyond individual components, Vossloh offers comprehensive solutions that integrate various technologies and strategies to manage noise at different stages of rail traffic operations.\n\n7. **Research and Development**: Continuous investment in R&D allows Vossloh to stay ahead in developing new technologies and materials that further reduce noise pollution. This includes collaboration with universities and research institutions to explore cutting-edge solutions.\n\nBy employing these technologies, Vossloh 