      "difficulty_id": "F-000009",
      "id": "train:000234:qa_pairs_factoid:0001",
      "problem": "Which measures were implemented to enhance energy efficiency and support renewable energy use in buildings?",
      "solution": "climate neutrality, climate-damaging emissions, electricity from renewable sources, energy efficiency, energy from renewable sources, green electricity strategy, photovoltaic systems, photovoltaics initiative, power purchase agreement, total capacity of approximately 3,400 KWp",
      "attempt": "To enhance energy efficiency and support the use of renewable energy in buildings, various measures have been implemented globally. These measures can be broadly categorized into policy initiatives, technological advancements, and financial incentives. Here are some key strategies:\n\n1. **Policy Initiatives:**\n   - **Building Codes and Standards:** Many countries have adopted or updated building codes that require higher levels of energy efficiency. For example, the U.S. has the ASHRAE 90.1 standard, while Europe has the Nearly Zero Energy Buildings (NZEB) directive.\n   - **Green Building Certifications:** Programs like LEED (Leadership in Energy and Environmental Design), BREEAM (Building Research Establishment Environmental Assessment Method), and Passive House standards encourage sustainable design and construction practices.\n\n2. **Technological Advancements:**\n   - **Energy-Efficient Appliances and Systems:** The development and adoption of more efficient HVAC systems, lighting, and appliances reduce overall energy consumption.\n   - **Smart Building Technologies:** Integration of smart technologies allows for better management of energy usage through automation and real-time monitoring.\n   - **Renewable Energy Systems:** Installation of solar panels, wind turbines, and geothermal systems provides clean energy directly from the building site.\n\n3. **Financial Incentives:**\n   - **Tax Credits and Rebates:** Governments offer tax credits, rebates, and grants to homeowners and businesses that invest in energy-efficient upgrades or renewable energy installations.\n   - **Low-Interest Loans:** Some regions provide low-interest loans specifically for energy-saving improvements and renewable energy projects.\n\n4. **Education and Awareness:**\n   - **Public Awareness Campaigns:** Educating the public about the benefits of energy efficiency and renewable energy can lead to increased demand for these solutions.\n   - **Training Programs:** Offering training programs for professionals in the construction and energy sectors ensures that they are equipped with the knowledge and skills needed to implement energy-efficient and renewable energy solutions effectively.\n\n5. **Research and Development:**\n   - **Investment in R&D:** Continued investment in research and development is crucial for discovering new materials, technologies, and methods that can further improve energy efficiency and the integration of renewable energy sources.\n\nThese measures collectively aim to reduce the environmental impact of buildings, lower energy costs, and promote sustainable living and working environments.",
      "grading": "No"
    },
