      "problem": "Which products and brands offer modular designs that facilitate sustainable lighting upgrades?",
      "solution": "OMEGA, PANOS, SLOTLIGHT, TECTON, Thorn lighting brand, Zumtobel lighting brand",
      "attempt": "Modular designs in lighting systems are becoming increasingly popular due to their sustainability benefits, including easier upgrades, reduced waste, and improved energy efficiency. Several brands and products are leading the way in this area:\n\n1. **Philips Hue**: Philips Hue offers a range of smart lights that can be easily upgraded with new bulbs or accessories without needing to replace the entire system. Their modular approach allows for flexibility in adding new features like color-changing capabilities or voice control.\n\n2. **Lutron Caseta**: Lutron's Caseta line includes a variety of dimmers, switches, and smart lighting controls that can be integrated into existing home wiring. This system is designed to be modular, allowing homeowners to add new devices as needed without replacing the whole setup.\n\n3. **Yeelight**: Yeelight provides smart LED bulbs and fixtures that can be controlled via Wi-Fi or Bluetooth. Their products are designed to be compatible with various smart home ecosystems, making it easy to upgrade or expand your lighting system over time.\n\n4. **LIFX**: Known for its high-quality smart LED bulbs, LIFX also offers a range of smart light strips and panels. These products are designed to be easily installed and can be controlled through a mobile app or voice commands, facilitating easy upgrades and customization.\n\n5. **Signify (formerly Philips Lighting)**: Signify offers a range of modular lighting solutions, particularly in commercial settings. Their Interact Office and Interact Landscaping systems allow for flexible installation and upgrades, supporting energy-efficient lighting in diverse environments.\n\n6. **Hubbell Lighting**: Hubbell Lighting provides a variety of commercial-grade modular lighting solutions that are designed for easy installation and maintenance. Their systems often include components that can be swapped out or upgraded individually, reducing waste and extending the life of the overall system.\n\n7. **Acuity Brands**: Acuity Brands offers several lines of modular lighting solutions, including outdoor and indoor fixtures. Their systems are designed to be adaptable, allowing for the integration of new technologies and features as they become available.\n\nThese brands not only focus on creating sustainable lighting options but also ensure that their products are designed with longevity and upgradability in mind, which is crucial for long-term sustainability in lighting systems.",
