      "solution": "Berlin, Frankfurt, Mainz, Munich, Regensburg, Vienna",
      "attempt": "CA Immo, a leading real estate company in Central and Eastern Europe, has been actively involved in implementing sustainable neighborhood development projects across several locations within its operational regions. Over the past two decades, some of the key areas where CA Immo has focused on sustainable urban development include:\n\n1. **Vienna, Austria**: One of the most notable projects is the redevelopment of the Favoriten district, where CA Immo has been working to create more sustainable living environments. This includes the integration of green spaces, energy-efficient buildings, and improved public transportation links.\n\n2. **Budapest, Hungary**: In Budapest, CA Immo has been involved in various projects aimed at revitalizing old neighborhoods while incorporating sustainable design principles. These efforts often focus on enhancing the quality of life for residents through better infrastructure and environmental sustainability.\n\n3. **Prague, Czech Republic**: The company has also undertaken initiatives in Prague that emphasize sustainable practices, such as the use of renewable energy sources and the creation of mixed-use developments that promote walkability and reduce reliance on private vehicles.\n\n4. **Warsaw, Poland**: Sustainable development projects in Warsaw have included the renovation of existing structures to meet modern energy efficiency standards and the construction of new buildings designed with sustainability in mind.\n\n5. **Other Cities Across CEE**: Beyond these major cities, CA Immo has also engaged in sustainable neighborhood development projects in other cities across Central and Eastern Europe, focusing on creating vibrant, livable communities that are environmentally responsible.\n\nThese projects typically involve a combination of residential, commercial, and recreational spaces, all designed to enhance the overall quality of life for residents while minimizing the environmental impact. CA Immo's approach to sustainable development often includes partnerships with local authorities, community groups, and other stakeholders to ensure that these projects not only meet current needs but also contribute positively to the long-term health and prosperity of the communities they serve.",
