      "question": "Why did the historical industrial activities on the CA Immo plot in Berlin result in significant environmental contamination, and how does this highlight the importance of sustainable industrial practices?",
      "answer": "The site housed a machine and metal goods factory and a coal lighter factory with melting pots for naphthalene between 1898 and 1982. These activities caused contamination of the soil and groundwater due to industrial processes and materials used.",
